The values is a list of 2, 1, and 3.
The lefts is a list of 1, -1, and -1.
The rights is a list of 2, -1, and -1.
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into queue.
The head is 0.
The count is 1.
The remaining is 1.
The levelcount is 1.
The nextcount is 0.
The depth is 0.
The bestdepth is 0.
The leftmost is item 0 of values.
Repeat while head is less than count.
The node is item head of queue.
Add 1 to head.
If remaining is levelcount and depth is more than bestdepth, set bestdepth to depth, set leftmost to item node of values.
If item node of lefts is at least 0, Place item node of lefts into queue, add 1 to count, add 1 to nextcount.
If item node of rights is at least 0, Place item node of rights into queue, add 1 to count, add 1 to nextcount.
Subtract 1 from remaining.
If remaining is 0, set remaining to nextcount, set levelcount to nextcount, set nextcount to 0, add 1 to depth.

Show leftmost.
